 - Fix/cleanup **incorrect char formatting**: e.g.; `"Berang�r"` -> `"Beranger"`; removed non-English hints.
 - Consolidated **long, unneeded, or unused comments** into [Long_Comments/](/Long_Comments/) and replaced them with short custom markers or files to keep code clean, lean, and readable. > ~500k characters reduced and still ongoing.
 - **BBAI logging is now XML-tunable:** BBAI AI-decision logging can now be enabled/disabled and adjusted through **SAS defines**, rather than editing and recompiling the DLL as in base AdvCiv. This is deemed valuable **not only for modders, but also for users** who can now view or generate `BBAI.log` files for review. Note: `LoggingEnabled=1` in `CivilizationIV.ini` is still required for Civ4 to write. This allowed for example to surgically identify and fix the root cause of a city not producing its first settler until ~T90 at normal game speed, which is way too late (`bWarPlan` was too aggressively gating settler production; now it only blocks settler production after early expansion has reached enough cities (inefficient at that point, better switch strategy)). Note: BBAI logs can be very long; for broad raw-log diagnosis, we usually give to an external LLM/AI such as ChatGPT the log file, as it is as of now agentic-token-free analysis (also good to give us a different point of view/review if needed).
-- **Timestamped BBAI log files:** Optionally log each new game and loaded save to a **new UTC-timestamped file** (e.g., `BBAI_20260705T071718Z_new1.log` or `BBAI_20260705T071718Z_load2.log`) instead of expanding the existing `BBAI.log`, which was very tedious to clean up or identify/store/read/review/upload, and so repeated save-file tests no longer require restarting Civ4. Each log begins notably with the new/load time, currently active BBAI log levels, turn/year, map and game settings (including `landheavy` and `navalheavy` actual game information), player counts, and RNG states, avoiding mixed logs and the need to restart Civ4 between repeated save-file tests. See also [README.md (BBAI logging head example)](/README.md#bbai-logging-head-example).
+- **Timestamped BBAI log files:** Optionally log each new game and loaded save to a **new UTC-timestamped file** (e.g., `BBAI_20260705T071718Z_new1.log` or `BBAI_20260705T071718Z_load2.log`) instead of expanding the existing `BBAI.log`, which was very tedious to clean up or identify/store/read/review/upload, and so repeated save-file tests no longer require restarting Civ4. Each log begins notably with the new/load time, currently active BBAI log levels, turn/year, map and game settings (including `landheavy` and `navalheavy` actual game information), player counts, and RNG states, avoiding mixed logs and the need to restart Civ4 between repeated save-file tests. See also [README.md (BBAI logging and head example)](/README.md#bbai-logging-and-head-example).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6022+) **SAS game-summary log:** added a separate `SASGameSummary_*.log` for compact autoplay and AI-strength review. It records high-level run context such as economy, expansion, city and battle history, worked plots, diplomacy, unit composition, and game state, complementing BBAI logs by summarizing what happened before or alongside detailed AI-decision traces. Note: it currently contains spoilers: a spoiler-free implementation was considered, so the human/active player can give to an LLM or such their play summary and get LLM or such suggestions or feedback/analysis, but it would require an extensive rework, so currently this is not supported; therefore, SAS game-summary log should as of now not be treated as a spoiler-free player-advice export. Note 2: depending on `SAS_GAME_SUMMARY_TURN_INTERVAL` value, the last turn may not appear in the log: for example, an autoplay run of 200 turns ends at T200 and thus does not seem to show the T200 data, only up to T190, so autoplay at least 201 turns to show T200 for example if you have this issue. See also [README.md (DLL Logging)](/README.md#dll-logging).
 - **BBAI worker log split:** added separate worker and Work Boat / `UNITAI_WORKER_SEA` BBAI log-level defines so ordinary `SAS_BBAI_UNIT_LOG_LEVEL` can focus on non-worker unit behavior such as scrapping, army movement, and combat-unit decisions. Worker and worker-sea logs had become noisy enough to hide those unit decisions, and Work Boats use distinct logic from land workers, so they now have their own category as well.
 - **BBAI Settler log split:** added `SAS_BBAI_SETTLER_LOG_LEVEL`, separated from UNIT so Settlers and other units can be inspected independently. This notably covers city-site decisions and Settler movement, scouting, returns, and founding; FOUND as of now separately controls detailed city-site scoring calculations. This notably lets UNIT investigate other unit behavior without enabling the multi-megabyte first-city Settler traces needed for example for the Berlin, Karakorum, and Cuzco regression tests.
 - **Culture-victory BBAI diagnostics:** added a new dedicated `SAS_BBAI_CULTURE_LOG_LEVEL` notably for diagnosing premature, uneven, or wasteful AI culture investment without enabling broad player/city logs. It records for example culture-stage reasons, current/projected Legendary-city countdowns and rival ranking, competing victory progress, actual culture-slider decisions, per-city weights and production, and culture contributed by production processes and assigned specialists.

